			'closing'         => '',
			'faqs'            => array(
				array( 'What makes IQ REM different from other real estate management software?', '<p>Unlike standalone real estate software, IQ REM is fully integrated with SAP Business One. This means your sales, billing, contracts, and financials all work from a single source of truth, reducing manual processes and enabling end-to-end visibility into your real estate business.</p>' ),
				array( 'Can IQ REM handle both residential and commercial property sales?', '<p>Yes. IQ REM is built to support diverse property types, including residential units, commercial spaces, buildings, and subdivisions. You can customize unit classifications, pricing schemes, and contract types based on your project needs.</p>' ),
				array( 'Can we generate reports on unit availability and sales performance?', '<p>Yes. IQ REM offers real-time dashboards and reporting tools that give you visibility into available inventory, sold units, customer payment status, and project performance, helping you make faster, data-driven decisions.</p>' ),
				array( 'Is IQ REM scalable as our real estate portfolio grows?', '<p>Definitely. DynamIQ’s IQ REM is built to scale with your operations—whether you’re handling one development or managing multiple projects and locations. You can add more properties, users, and workflows as needed without disrupting your existing setup.</p>' ),
				array( 'How long does it take to implement IQ REM for an existing SAP B1 user?', '<p>Typical implementation can take a few weeks, depending on the complexity of your real estate operations and the volume of historical data to be migrated. We conduct discovery, configuration, training, and testing to ensure a smooth rollout.</p>' ),
				array( 'Is customer data secure in the system?', '<p>Yes. The IQ REM module follows SAP Business One’s security protocols, including user access controls and audit trails. Sensitive customer, financial, and property data is protected at every stage of the workflow.</p>' ),
